  {
   "title": "वाक्य की बनावट ✍️",
   "text": "Hindi sentence = कर्ता (doer) + कर्म (object) + क्रिया (action): 'राम ने आम खाया' — the order matters!",
   "emoji": "✍️",
   "bgColor": "from-indigo-400 to-purple-500",
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "title": "ने and को 🎭",
   "text": "'ने' follows the doer: 'राम ने खाया'. 'को' follows the object: 'आम को खाया' — they mark the roles!",
   "emoji": "🎭",
   "bgColor": "from-blue-400 to-cyan-500",
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "title": "शब्द-क्रम — Word Order 🔄",
   "text": "'बच्चा खेल खेलता है' (child plays game) — Hindi order is doer + object + action, not like English!",
   "emoji": "🔄",
   "bgColor": "from-green-400 to-emerald-500",
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "title": "वचन — One or Many 🔢",
   "text": "लड़का (one boy) → लड़के (many boys); किताब → किताबें — the ending changes for plural!",
   "emoji": "🔢",
   "bgColor": "from-orange-400 to-amber-500",
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "title": "वाक्य बनाओ 🏗️",
   "text": "Doer + ने + Object + को + Action: 'मीना ने पानी पिया' — you built a real Hindi sentence!",
   "emoji": "🏗️",
   "bgColor": "from-pink-400 to-rose-500",
   "spoken": ""
  }
